WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.033
Barbados scored an own goal

2
00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:02.833
on purpose.

3
00:00:02.833 --> 00:00:04.067
Then they defended

4
00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:04.867
both goals.

5
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:07.333
It was a Caribbean Cup

6
00:00:07.333 --> 00:00:08.567
qualifier in 1994.

7
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.233
And winning the match

8
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:11.033
wasn't enough.

9
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.833
Barbados needed to win

10
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:14.767
by two goals to qualify.

11
00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.500
Late in the game,

12
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.767
they led two-one.

13
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.500
A win—but still elimination.

14
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.800
They could try

15
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.867
to score again.

16
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.700
Or exploit an unusual rule.

17
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.767
A draw at full time

18
00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:26.900
meant extra time.

19
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.167
The first goal there

20
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.433
would end the match—and

21
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:30.033
count double.

22
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.700
So, one goal in extra time

23
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.933
could give Barbados

24
00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.167
the two-goal margin

25
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:35.967
they needed.

26
00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.233
They deliberately scored

27
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.667
into their own net.

28
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:39.033
Two-two.

29
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.500
Now they just needed

30
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.967
to keep it tied.

31
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.700
But Grenada had spotted

32
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.433
a way to stop them.

33
00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:47.267
Score against Barbados,

34
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.900
and Grenada wins.

35
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.967
Score into their own goal,

36
00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.200
and Grenada loses

37
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.700
by only one—still
enough to qualify.

38
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.100
Before full time,

39
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.733
either goal would do.

40
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.100
Barbados had to protect

41
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.100
their own goal—and
Grenada's.

42
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.200
The opponent's net

43
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.267
had become something

44
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.667
they needed to defend.

45
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.500
They kept it two-two

46
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.733
until full time.

47
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:10.433
Then Barbados scored

48
00:01:10.433 --> 00:01:11.933
the extra-time winner.

49
00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:12.600
It counted

50
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.933
as a two-goal victory.

51
00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:15.367
They qualified.

52
00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.867
Scoring against themselves

53
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:18.567
hadn't been the mistake.

54
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:19.733
It was their way

55
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:20.933
of making the rules

56
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:21.833
work for them.
